    {
      "question": "Why is masking used in the decoder self-attention?",
      "expected": "prevent attending to subsequent positions",
      "answer": "Masking is used in the decoder self-attention to prevent positions from attending to subsequent positions [1]. This prevents leftward information flow in the decoder to preserve the auto-regressive property [2]. Combined with the fact that output embeddings are offset by one position, this ensures that the predictions for position i can depend only on the known outputs at positions less than i [1].",
